# refined-checks.bot -- repeated refined-type predicates: an outer
# Emailish? check whose result is re-checked in the then branch
# (statically redundant), and UriQueryValue? on a value whose type proves
# the answer.
#
# Canonical surface-Botlish source (CANONICAL-SURFACE-BENCHMARKS.md);
# migrated from the historical raw-core-IR fixture bench/refined-checks.ir,
# which remains in bench/ only as a frozen input for historical audit-
# reproduction tooling (see that report) -- it is no longer canonical
# benchmark source. Spelled with the canonical predicate name emailish?
# (lib/web.tcl, R2-ORDINARY-EMAILISH-PREDICATE.md) rather than the
# deprecated Emailish? compatibility alias that the old .ir fixture used
# (that alias exists specifically to keep the frozen .ir spelling working,
# and is untouched by this migration -- see native/native.tcl).
#
# The first check's string is a Unicode-forcing case, not ASCII-only: "é"
# (local part), "例え" (a domain label) and "テスト" (the TLD) are all
# non-ASCII letters that emailish?'s Tcl-compatible [:alpha:]/[:alnum:]
# classes accept -- see NATIVE-TCL-UNICODE.md.
#
# requires: web
#
# expect: [400, 0]

q = uriEscape("a b")

fn check(n, acc, s, q):
    if n <= 0:
        return acc
    hit = if emailish?(s):
        if emailish?(s):
            if UriQueryValue?(q):
                1
            else:
                0
        else:
            0
    else:
        0
    check(n - 1, acc + hit, s, q)

[check(400, 0, "café@例え.テスト", q), check(400, 0, "not-an-email", q)]
